use flake

# A host toolchain manager (mise) exports GOROOT/GOBIN for its own Go on every
# prompt. A GOROOT from the host that survives into the dev shell makes the Nix
# `go` run the host's `compile` binary, failing with
# `compile: version X does not match go tool version Y`.
# Unsetting it here (rather than re-pointing it in the flake) also covers the
# hook-order case: direnv re-applies the unset whenever a later prompt export
# puts GOROOT back.
unset GOROOT GOBIN
